<chapter xml:id="chapter-multivariate-differential-calculus" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Multivariate Differential Calculus</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter extends differential calculus from functions of one variable to functions of
      several variables.
      The central objects are partial derivatives, the gradient, and the Hessian matrix,
      which together provide the tools for analysing rates of change, approximating functions
      locally, and locating extrema in higher dimensions.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="functions-continuity-partial-derivatives/section.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="error-propagation-taylor-extrema/section.ptx"/>

</chapter>
